# CRUD configuration

## Plugin semantics

Many behaviors are expressible via Crud component/action configuration (enabled actions, related models, messages, find methods, etc.). Prefer documented config keys for the installed version.

## Required behavior

- Check CRUD docs/config for the installed major before writing a listener.
- Keep configuration discoverable (controller initialize / shared AppController patterns as the project already does).
- Escalate to events only when config cannot express the need.

## Anti-patterns

- Custom listeners that only set values already supported by config
- Inventing undocumented config keys
